traceability.evidence:
1) Dedicated tests for this story exist and pass: - File: tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts - Header: """ /** * Tests for: docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md * @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING - Verify ESLint --fix automatically adds missing @story annotations to functions * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT - Verify ESLint --fix corrects simple annotation format issues for @story annotations */ """ - Tests for REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING: - Valid cases ensure already annotated function/method are unchanged. - Invalid cases assert ESLint fixes to: - `function autoFixMe() {}` → `/** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */
function autoFixMe() {}` - `const fnExpr = function() {};` → `/** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */
const fnExpr = function() {};` - `class C {
 method() {}
}` → `class C {
 /** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */
 method() {}
}` - `declare function tsDecl(): void;` and TS interface method signatures, with matching expected output. - Tests for REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT (valid-annotation-format): - Valid: already-correct path `// @story docs/stories/005.0-DEV-EXAMPLE.story.md` is unchanged. - Invalid: auto-fix path suffixes - `.story` → `.story.md` - no extension → `.story.md`.
2) Jest test run (npm test -- --verbose) shows all tests passing, including the story-specific suite: - Output excerpt: """ PASS tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts Auto-fix behavior (Story 008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX) [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] require-story-annotation auto-fix require-story-annotation --fix valid ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] already annotated function is unchanged ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] already annotated class method is unchanged invalid ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] adds @story before function declaration when missing ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] adds @story before function expression when missing ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] adds @story before class method when missing ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] adds @story before TS declare function when missing ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] adds @story before TS method signature when missing [REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] valid-annotation-format auto-fix valid-annotation-format --fix simple @story extension issues valid ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] already-correct story path is unchanged invalid ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] adds .md extension for .story path ✓ [REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] adds .story.md extension when missing entirely """ - Overall Jest summary: "Test Suites: 35 passed, 35 total; Tests: 266 passed, 266 total".
3) Implementation of require-story-annotation auto-fix matches REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING / SAFE / PRESERVE: - File: src/rules/require-story-annotation.ts - Meta configuration: """ meta: { type: "problem", docs: { description: "Require @story annotations on functions and auto-fix missing annotations where possible", recommended: "error", }, hasSuggestions: true, /** * Auto-fix support for inserting @story annotations. * * @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md * @req REQ-ANNOTATION-REQUIRED * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING - `fixable: "code"` is used to implement REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING for missing @story annotations. * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE - Auto-fix is conservative and only adds a single-line JSDoc @story annotation without modifying existing runtime expressions. * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE - Auto-fix behavior preserves surrounding code formatting and indentation when inserting the placeholder JSDoc. */ fixable: "code", messages: { missingStory: "Function '{{name}}' must have an explicit @story annotation. Add a JSDoc or line comment with @story that points to the implementing story file (for example, docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md).", }, ... } """ - Rule file clearly declares traceability back to 008.0: """ * @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md * @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING ... * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE ... * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE ... """ - The tests exercise that the auto-fix adds exactly one single-line `@story` JSDoc comment and leaves function bodies untouched, matching REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, and REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE.
4) Implementation of valid-annotation-format auto-fix matches REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT / SAFE / PRESERVE: - File: src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts - Key helpers: - `createStoryFix(context, comment, fixed)` (annotated with Story 008.0 and REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE / PRESERVE) locates only the `@story` value substring inside the comment text and returns a fixer that: - Computes a precise `fixRange` within the comment: `[start + valueStartInComment, start + valueEndInComment]`. - Returns `null` when the tag or value range cannot be safely determined (guards for TAG_NOT_FOUND_INDEX and missing match), thereby avoiding unsafe edits. - `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix(...)` (annotated with Story 008.0 and REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT / SAFE / PRESERVE) uses `createStoryFix` and: - Falls back to reporting without a fix when `fixFactory` is falsy (unfixable/ambiguous), satisfying the error-handling criterion. - Otherwise attaches `fix: fixFactory()` to the ESLint report, so only the path substring is replaced. - `validateStoryAnnotation(...)` computes `fixed = getFixedStoryPath(collapsed)` and applies a fix only when: - `fixed` is non-null and - the configured `pathPattern` matches `fixed`. If not, it reports without fix. - Rule meta.fixable is limited to code-level suffix normalization and explicitly linked to Story 008.0: """ meta: { ... /** * This rule's fixable support is limited to safe @story path suffix normalization per Story 008.0. * Fixes are limited strictly to adjusting the suffix portion of the @story path (e.g., adding * `.md` or `.story.md`), preserving all other comment text and whitespace exactly as written. * * @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE * @req REQ-REGEX-VALIDATION - Ensure regex configuration does not affect fix safety * @req REQ-BACKWARD-COMP - Maintain previous auto-fix behavior under invalid configs */ fixable: "code", }, """ - This matches REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE, and the acceptance criteria around safe, non-destructive suffix-only fixes.
5) Documentation coverage for auto-fix behavior (Documentation acceptance criterion): - File: user-docs/api-reference.md - `traceability/require-story-annotation` section explicitly documents auto-fix: """ When run with `--fix`, the rule inserts a single-line placeholder JSDoc `@story` annotation above missing functions, methods, TypeScript declare functions, and interface method signatures using a built-in template aligned with Story 008.0. This template is currently fixed but structured for future configurability, and fixes are strictly limited to adding this placeholder annotation without altering the function body or changing any runtime behavior. """ - `traceability/valid-annotation-format` section similarly documents its limited auto-fix behavior: """ When run with `--fix`, the rule limits changes to safe `@story` path suffix normalization only—for example, adding `.md` when the path ends with `.story`, or adding `.story.md` when the base path has no extension—using targeted replacements implemented in the `getFixedStoryPath` and `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix` helpers. It does not change directories, infer new story names, or modify any surrounding comment text or whitespace, in line with Story 008.0; more advanced path normalization strategies and selective toggles to enable or disable specific auto-fix behaviors are not yet implemented. """ - These docs match the scope described in the story and explain what `--fix` does and the safety constraints.
6) Alignment with story requirements and scope: - REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING: Implemented by `require-story-annotation` with `fixable: "code"` and exercised by RuleTester cases that assert exact before/after behavior for functions, class methods, TS declare functions, and interface methods. - REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT: Implemented via `getFixedStoryPath` and `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix` in `valid-annotation-format`, with tests confirming `.story` → `.story.md` and missing extension → `.story.md` fixes. - REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE / REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE: Both rules only add a new JSDoc comment or adjust the `@story` path substring; they never change function bodies or other code, and they abort fixes when the path location cannot be safely determined. - REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE and REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE are explicitly marked in the story as "Not yet implemented" and described as future enhancements; they are not part of the acceptance criteria and their absence matches the documented current-scope behavior.
Given the dedicated passing tests keyed to this story, the rule implementations with explicit fix support, safe-fix logic and fallbacks, and user documentation describing the exact `--fix` behavior for both rules, all checked acceptance criteria for Story 008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX are satisfied.
